Reading 2a: lines 196-209 are the http adapter. Its try (196) closes at the
`on http.ClientException` clause (199), which only rethrows a transport
failure; `throw ServerException` (209) sits after that block, so nothing
catches it inside the snippet. Lines 298-303 are the Result -> Exceptions
"Update UI handling" After: it catches AuthException and others from the use
case and throws nothing. snippet-test.log runs the adapter: a 500 and a 404
surface as ServerException, not NetworkException.
